dience and satisfies legal requirements. | axe-core, Lighthouse accessibility audit. |\n| **13. Write tests** | • Unit tests for components and reducers.<br>• Integration tests for API calls.<br>• End‑to‑end tests for checkout flow. | Reduces regressions and gives confidence when refactoring. | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress for E2E. |\n| **14. Continuous integration & deployment** | • Push commits to GitHub → run CI pipeline (lint, test, build).<br>• Deploy to Netlify, Vercel, or Render. | Automation speeds releases and catches errors early. | GitHub Actions, Netlify CI, Vercel Pipelines. |\n| **15. Monitor & iterate** | • Add analytics (Google Analytics, Plausible).<br>• Track conversion funnels and drop‑off points.<br>• Gather user feedback via surveys or heatmaps. | Data‑driven decisions improve UX and revenue. | Google Analytics, Hotjar, Mixpanel. |\n\n---\n\n### Quick‑Start Checklist\n\n1. **Create repo** → `git init` + GitHub template.\n2. **Scaffold** → `npm create vite@latest my-shop --template react-ts`.\n3. **Install core libs** → `npm i axios @reduxjs/toolkit react-redux tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer`.\n4. **Set up Tailwind** → `npx tailwindcss init -p` + configure `tailwind.config.js`.\n5. **Add Redux Toolkit** → `npx reduxjs/toolkit` + create slices (`cartSlice.ts`, `authSlice.ts`).\n6. **Add API services** → `src/api/products.ts` with Axios instance.\n7. **Add routing** → `react-router-dom` + define routes in `App.tsx`.\n8. **Add auth** → `npm i @auth0/auth0-react` or set up custom JWT flow.\n9. **Add Stripe** → `npm i @stripe/react-stripe-js @stripe/stripe-js`.\n10. **Run dev** → `npm run dev` → start building components.\n\n---\n\n### Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n| Pitfall | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| **Hard‑coding API URLs** | Use environment variables (`VITE_API_URL`) and a config file. |\n| **Storing JWT in localStorage** | Prefer HttpOnly cookies or secure storage; mitigate XSS. |\n| **Large bundle size** | Tree‑shake unused imports, l